CloudBurrow patch 5 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1138); needs patches 0001 and 0004.

The bug: patch 0004 writes a GEOGRAPHY given as WKT text in BigQuery's
form (POINT(1 2), GEOMETRYCOLLECTION EMPTY) only at a row's top level; one
inside a RECORD, a REPEATED column or a REPEATED RECORD of a streamed row
or a load was stored as given (POINT (1 2)). The patch writes it so at any
depth, in decodeBytesValues, which already walks every nested value of a
row for BYTES. The numbers of the text are still kept as written
(POINT(1.0 2) is not written POINT(1 2)).
internal/contentdata/geography_nested_test.go fails without the patch.

